## [:< ##

# name  = plugin.user-edit.address-cluster.tab_info
# descr = address-cluster plugin's self-description
# param = -none-

## pins 'address' -- the SAME real optional field users.record.optional_fields
## already declares
## [ see user-edit-address-cluster-plugin.yaml's storage_shape ]. per
## plugin.user-edit.example.tab_info's own hard-earned lesson [ REAL BUG,
## 2b504e4ef : a throwaway test plugin pinned a real field by accident and
## silently made it readonly-until-entered for every user ] -- here that is
## not an accident, it is the entire point : this plugin's job is to take the
## plain-scalar 'address' field over completely and give it a structured,
## multi-entry meaning instead.
##
## COLLISION CHECK, per the design doc's own reminder : 'address' does not
## collide with plugin.user-edit.example's own pin [ 'example_test_field' ],
## the only other plugin currently wired into plugins.load.
return {
    qw| label |       => qw| addresses |,
    qw| pinned_keys | => [qw| address |],
};

